# Functions over the complexity limits, frozen 2026-09-15 when this repo turned
# the hub's --ratchets on.
#
# Format: <path> | <function> | <metric: cc|nesting> | <count> | <reason>
#
# cc = cyclomatic complexity (limit 15); nesting = block depth relative to the
# function body (limit 5). Same four-way contract as function-size.allow: growth,
# a new offender, an unrecorded shrink and a stale freeze all fail.
# third_party/ANTfrastructure/docs/code-quality-tooling.md#shell-complexity-code-complexity
#
# Most rows are the benchmark port. Most are TABLES -- one arm per option, per
# rule, per schema field, per hardware fact -- where the number is a count of real
# cases and collapsing it would delete the case. The three that are not are
# bench_coding.evaluate, bench_compare.compare and bench_tools.evaluate, each of
# which already has a row in function-size.allow and one seam that would answer both.

benchmarks/bench_agent.py | main | cc | 27 | baseline 2026-09-15: the agent CLI's flag dispatch -- one branch per option and per candidate-resolution fallback. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them
benchmarks/bench_agent.py | old_name_uses | cc | 23 | baseline 2026-09-15: the compatibility scan for renamed tools; one branch per historical spelling it still has to recognise. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them
benchmarks/bench_agent.py | self_test | cc | 18 | baseline 2026-09-15: the lane's own pre-flight -- one arm per precondition it refuses to start without. Branch count is the precondition count. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them
benchmarks/bench_coding.py | _bound_names | cc | 18 | baseline 2026-09-15: an AST walk with one arm per binding node kind. A visitor table in disguise; collapsing it would hide the node list. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them
benchmarks/bench_coding.py | ask | cc | 19 | baseline 2026-09-15: the streaming request's failure modes -- deadline, give-up, empty delta, missing finish_reason, transport error. Every branch is a measured case. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them
benchmarks/bench_coding.py | check_forbidden | cc | 19 | baseline 2026-09-15: one arm per forbidden construct the grader refuses. A rule table. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them
benchmarks/bench_coding.py | evaluate | cc | 80 | baseline 2026-09-15: the worst number in the repo, and the same body function-size.allow already queues at 340 lines. One fix serves both: extract grade-one-task. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them; 2026-09-24 (review pass): +2 -- a spacer request before each repeat (GenieX answers an identical follow-up along a cache path that changes the reply) and effective_n taken from the cases when every repeat agrees on pass/fail; 2026-09-24 (roadmap integration): +9 -- P1.2 prompt variants: the per-phrasing loop, the spacer only between identical follow-ups and the spread record; P7.6 PowerShell
benchmarks/bench_coding.py | extract_code | cc | 21 | baseline 2026-09-15: fenced-block extraction with the AST-first/regex-fallback ladder the 2026-09-05 review prescribed. Each rung is a real model output shape. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them
benchmarks/bench_coding.py | main | cc | 34 | baseline 2026-09-15: task-set selection plus the sweep dispatch; pairs with the 263-line row in function-size.allow. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them; 2026-09-24 (roadmap integration): +4 -- --prompt-variants and P1.5 run-start record: one tool_files tuple and run_start() before the first request; 2026-09-24 (roadmap2): -1 -- the 'if suspect and args.prompt_variants' rescore branch is gone
benchmarks/bench_compare.py | compare | cc | 62 | baseline 2026-09-15: the comparison report rendered in sequence -- one branch per printed section and per optional column. Pairs with the 215-line row. the benchmark port from the hub's linux/llm-stack, behaviour-frozen at import; a decomposition must land behind the measurement tests, not ahead of them; 2026-09-24 (review pass): +2 -- the contract-report refusal and the NOTHING COMPARED count; 2026-09-24 (roadmap2): 65 -> 62: the per-attempt-time and lane-throughput SLOWER/faster arms moved into compare_verdict.LoadGate.judge and _throughput_line
